# DYN Pallets — Cline Project Rules

Before editing, inspect the relevant files and preserve the existing visual system, routes, content architecture, and responsive behavior.

## Repository safety
- Never modify `.git`, Git remotes, branches, commit history, repository URLs, credentials, GitHub settings, or deployment connections.
- Never run `git init`, `git remote set-url`, `git reset --hard`, `git clean -fd`, force-push, or destructive Git commands.
- Do not commit or push unless the user explicitly asks.

## Editing rules
- Make only changes required by the current task.
- Do not redesign unrelated sections.
- Reuse existing components, data structures, CSS variables, and naming conventions.
- Preserve Next.js App Router structure and existing URLs.
- Keep TypeScript strictness and accessibility attributes intact.
- Do not expose secrets or write API keys into tracked files.

## Validation
After code changes, run the least-destructive checks available:
1. `npm run lint`
2. `npm run build`
Fix errors caused by your changes. Do not change unrelated code just to silence pre-existing warnings.

At the end, summarize modified files and what changed.
